A wallet you can't get locked out of. A trust layer for AI agents. Ten bridges behind a single door. A pop culture legend gone onchain.

That is the newest stretch of the Hashlock client list, and we could not be happier about it.

@unifi_x is making selfcustody a lot less scary. Their smart account system means a lost key no longer means lost funds: a passkey plus a set of trusted guardians can restore access to your wallet. We worked through the recovery contracts that make it possible.

OpenMatter Network is building verifiable compute for the agentic economy. Zero knowledge proofs, secure multiparty computation, and quantum resistant cryptography so organizations can prove what happened instead of trusting it did. Exactly the kind of codebase our auditors love to sink into.

@LucidLabsFi is untangling one of Web3's oldest headaches: bridge fragmentation. One integration routes stablecoins through ten different bridges, always picking the best path for the job, while idle liquidity earns yield that flows back to the ecosystems that hold it. We audited the asset controller at the heart of those flows.

@DeLoreanlabs took one of the most iconic brands in automotive history and built a real onchain ecosystem around it. We are proud to be working on the staking and governance contracts behind $DMC.

Four teams, four wildly different visions, one shared call: build with security from day one. Welcome aboard 🔒

#Web3Security #SmartContractAudit #Blockchain #DeFi
